  <notes>
    Verified-complete (2026-07-09, this session). The implementation was already fully landed in a
    prior session's "016/030/032 integration wave" (2026-07-08, see project current-task.md) — this
    task-execute pass re-grounded in code, re-ran the corrected-contract checks the invoking prompt
    specified, and confirmed nothing further was needed. No new edits made this pass.

    CONTRACT CORRECTION already applied at authoring time (Spike 0, 2026-07-08): the POML's
    `compose_action_request` PaneEventBus discriminant never existed and was never added. Confirmed
    by repo-wide grep — every remaining occurrence of the string is an explanatory code comment
    (in ComposeEditor.tsx, ComposeAiToolbar.tsx, ComposeWorkspace.tsx, useSerialActionQueue.ts)
    stating it was retracted / must not be added; zero live discriminant/type/dispatch exists.

    ACTUAL DISPATCH SEAM: `ComposeAiToolbar.tsx` calls a bound `dispatchConsumer(bindingId, { slots })`
    (`createConsumerDispatcher` from `@spaarke/ui-components`, mirroring
    `useConsumerChips.tsx`'s pattern) built via `useMemo` from `bffBaseUrl`/`sessionId`/`useAuth()`/the
    inherited `dispatch` PaneEventBus function. When the host supplies the FR-18
    `enqueueComposeAction` prop (threaded ComposeEditor -> ComposeAiToolbar), the click instead calls
    `enqueueComposeAction({ id, bindingId, args })`, routing through the host's serial queue
    (task 032); otherwise it falls back to the toolbar's own `dispatchConsumer` call. The toolbar
    itself makes NO PaneEventBus emission and NO direct HTTP call — `dispatchConsumer`/
    `enqueueComposeAction` own the actual POST to
    `/api/ai/chat/sessions/{sessionId}/dispatch` (ADR-039).

    Files (already in place, verified this pass — none newly created/modified):
    - `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeAiToolbar.tsx` — the floating
      AI toolbar; extensible action registry (`getComposeAiToolbarActions`/
      `registerComposeAiToolbarAction`, replace-by-id); 3 primary actions (Explain/Compare/Draft, all
      `bindingId: ''` Phase-4 stubs, rendered disabled per the "honest stub" rule) + "More actions…"
      overflow menu.
    - `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx` — mounts
      `ComposeAiToolbar` inside the existing `BubbleMenu` render prop (the "AI TOOLBAR MOUNT" region);
      threads `enqueueComposeAction` through from its own props.
    - `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeAiToolbar.test.tsx` —
      co-located RTL suite, 10/10 passing (render/negative-collapsed/no-editor/disabled-stub;
      light+dark no-hardcoded-hex; wired-dispatch call-shape; stub-does-not-dispatch;
      registry-extensibility via `registerComposeAiToolbarAction`; empty-overflow placeholder).
    - `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-contracts.ts` — NOT modified;
      no `compose_action_request` discriminant added (per the corrected contract). The POML's
      referenced `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/types/compose-contracts.ts` path does not exist /
      was stale; the shared-lib path is canonical (already noted in ComposeEditor.tsx's JSDoc).

    Verification run this pass: `npx tsc --noEmit` in `Spaarke.Compose.Components` — clean. Full
    package `npx jest` — 6 suites / 53 tests passing (matches the prior session's recorded 53/53,
